{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "002W", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{J}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{J}$", "MATH_0005": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\times \\mathcal{J} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0006": "$(i, j) \\mapsto M_{i, j}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{categories-lemma-directed-commutes}\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:04d593106f9643fa49ce904773bef092a3560d3de3c8ac3a61a077e7ac6e4f8e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49fa69a204e9666dd946d276c0c26ccf3a33c1ed66962200fe34661bec177744", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be index categories. Assume that <MATH_0003> is filtered and <MATH_0004> is finite. Let <MATH_0005>, <MATH_0006> be a diagram of diagrams of sets. In this case", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0b0da01fe57b5d7751c8cb1117263b8f642dee8248936a64a65f57a639185f69", "unit_id": "tag:002W:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "display_math", "parent_tag": "002W", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\colim_i \\lim_j M_{i, j}\n=\n\\lim_j \\colim_i M_{i, j}.\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:800c284e0e644844fa1ed110ec48c98a8cd9fbaaf0b1f45f2abdaf3857ded50d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:720877dd06ce8de46ef352cb5cf6a95301d633f60f3ab93de3c6e61c9bcf2031", "source_text": "<MATH_0001>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f624e62d0a08cb4d4f7609fd8d992c88c0c527d3d910b8338b5f898e6261de67", "unit_id": "tag:002W:display001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002W", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{lemma}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:296abd71dcc1d247eb0b884c877ab599801903e77dbd3fe3ed7161922082833d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:70f81d62aa7eb2e92ede7eda94fa9d186cd6bb453b1b609118e1937874ce5392", "source_text": "In particular, colimits over <MATH_0001> commute with finite products, fibre products, and equalizers of sets.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d8877b56edd1894535892720af109798f4d073b66a60425cb7106d0b20575e07", "unit_id": "tag:002W:p001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "002W", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{proof}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2a4d6ef266c6163f4a66dff91e9025dd539ffce369d04bb4dc14a2e44c17cd99", "source_text": "Omitted. In fact, it is a fun exercise to prove that a category is filtered if and only if colimits over the category commute with finite limits (into the category of sets).", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dc95edebf6ce32cd4d01bc3b18758607a6b7f7851ef344a17312a71cd3736ec9", "unit_id": "tag:002W:proof-p001"}
